		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Penetration]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=4348#p4348"><![CDATA[
This to be precise, Bullet uses EPA by default, it give an exact penetration depth (within a given tolerance). Sampling method is an approximation.<br><br>Apart from SAT, which is also exact, other methods to approximate penetration depth include <a href="http://www.cs.unc.edu/~geom/DEEP/" class="postlink">Dual-space Expansion</a><br><br>Benefit of EPA over SAT is that it support non-polyhedral convex objects like implicit cylinders &amp; cones, convex sum of objects, minkowski sum etc.<br><br>Hope this helps,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Tue May 29, 2007 11:49 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
